Third-party components used by n2kd
===================================

nlohmann/json
  License: MIT
  Source: https://github.com/nlohmann/json
  Used as a header-only library compiled into n2kd.

canboat PGN database (canboat.json)
  License: Apache-2.0 (full text in canboat-LICENSE)
  Source: https://github.com/canboat/canboat
  Distributed unmodified as usr/share/cheekymarine/canboat.json.

Catch2
  License: BSL-1.0
  Source: https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2
  Used only to build the unit tests. Not distributed in release tarballs.

Statically linked runtime (aarch64 release tarball only)
--------------------------------------------------------

The aarch64 n2kd binary is fully statically linked and contains:

GNU C Library (glibc)
  License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
libstdc++ and libgcc (GCC runtime libraries)
  License: GPL-3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception

The corresponding source for these libraries is available from the Ubuntu
24.04 cross-toolchain packages used to build the binary (gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu,
g++-aarch64-linux-gnu, libc6-dev-arm64-cross and their source packages). To
allow relinking against a modified C library, the object files n2kd was built
from are available on request from the project maintainer.

The x86_64 release tarball links these libraries dynamically from the host
system.
